pr_comments:
I [rebased this branch](https://github.com/dacap/aseprite/tree/show-output-folder) again to the latest beta commit to fix the conflict. I was able to test this on Windows too (and [found a bug](https://github.com/aseprite/laf/commit/07f4e9577d67aed16bd04efd545a18aa26e2037e) in `get_absolute_path()`).

It looks great! I really like how it's working this now. There are a couple of changes I'd made (probably you can `rebase --interactive` to edit the commits):

1. About https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/pull/4873/commits/8d2f0380d97b03e58a368dd8fecb41a793879cba, we can add the `basepath` argument but without these specials `{doc}` or `{cwd}` modifiers, as the user already can access these fields from [app.sprite.filename](https://www.aseprite.org/api/sprite#spritefilename) and [app.fs.currentPath](https://www.aseprite.org/api/app_fs#appfscurrentpath), and the "doc" term is not used in scripting (only "sprite"), but it's better if we keep this parameter simple, and in this way we avoid adding a new kind of filename formatting (which means more documentation).
2. Remove `FilenameFieldObserver` class, and do the `Preferences::instance().general.editFullPath.AfterChange.connect()` inside `FilenameField::FilenameField(...)` constructor. Remember to create a `obs::scoped_connection` member in `FilenameField` so this observer is disconnected automatically in its destructor. E.g. You can find some examples in the `Editor`: [m_fgColorChangeConn](https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/5e6927ed4e362c42ce8a3aecb62e6f64a3c8a5a5/src/app/ui/editor/editor.h#L442), and [connect() call](https://github.com/aseprite/aseprite/blob/5e6927ed4e362c42ce8a3aecb62e6f64a3c8a5a5/src/app/ui/editor/editor.cpp#L178-L179).
3. In `FilenameField::onBrowse()` you can select the `relative` or `absolute` item depending on the current `Preferences::instance().general.editFullPath()` value to display a checkbox in the current option, e.g.:
   ```diff
   diff --git a/src/app/ui/filename_field.cpp b/src/app/ui/filename_field.cpp
   index 5fd0e7823..8bc248371 100644
   --- a/src/app/ui/filename_field.cpp
   +++ b/src/app/ui/filename_field.cpp
   @@ -124,6 +124,10 @@ void FilenameField::onBrowse()
      ui::MenuItem choose(Strings::select_file_choose());
      ui::MenuItem relative(Strings::select_file_relative_path(m_pathBase));
      ui::MenuItem absolute(Strings::select_file_absolute_path());
   +
   +  relative.setSelected(!m_editFullPath);
   +  absolute.setSelected(m_editFullPath);
   +
      menu.addChild(&choose);
      menu.addChild(new ui::MenuSeparator());
      menu.addChild(&relative); 
   ```
   ![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3b5ec3fc-c703-4e65-a5d2-9a60c89f6f66)
   In this way the user can expect a "do nothing" action if the current checked option is selected again from the menu.

